		<p class="professional-summary-text">
			I am Head of Open Source Engineering at Harper, where I led the company's
			transition from a closed-source product to an open-source-first platform.
			This means owning the dual-license model (Apache 2.0 core with a
			source-available pro tier), building contribution procedures, and growing
			a developer community grounded in trust and transparency.
		</p>
		<p class="professional-summary-text">
			Outside of Harper, I am a Node.js core contributor and Undici maintainer.
			I represent the Node.js and JavaScript ecosystem in the OpenJS Foundation
			and WinterTC (ECMA TC55), where I work on standards and community
			development for web-interoperable runtimes. I have spoken at JSConf NA and
			NodeConf EU. I also support open source sustainability directly as a donor
			to the <Link href="https://endowment.dev">Open Source Endowment</Link>.
		</p>
		<p class="professional-summary-text">
			Previous roles include Senior Software Engineer at Vercel, where I worked
			on the core build platform and contributed performance improvements to
			Next.js, and Software Engineer II at Microsoft, where I built enterprise
			Azure solutions for large partners. Outside of work, I am a certified ski
			instructor at Breckenridge, a Protect Our Winters member, and a volunteer
			with outdoor education programs in Summit County, Colorado. I care about
			climate and environmental stewardship, and I am particularly drawn to
			working with companies building in that space. I take on select consulting
			engagements through <Link href="https://alpinemooseinnovations.com"
				>Alpine Moose Innovations</Link
			> and am open to early-stage investing conversations. Reach me at <Link
				href="mailto:ethan@arrowood.dev">ethan@arrowood.dev</Link
			>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="talks" class="talks-container">
		<SectionHeading id="talks" class="sub-title">Talks</SectionHeading>
		<div>
			<h3 class="talks-sub-heading">Upcoming</h3>
			{
				upcomingTalks.length > 0 ? (
					<ul class="upcoming-talks-list">
						{upcomingTalks.map((talk) => (
							<li class="upcoming-talk-item">
								<p class="upcoming-talk-title">
									<Link href={talk.url}>{talk.frontmatter.title}</Link>
								</p>
								<p class="upcoming-talk-description">
									{talk.frontmatter.description}
								</p>
								<ul class="upcoming-talk-events">
									{talk.frontmatter.events
										.filter((event) => new Date(event.date) >= now)
										.map((event: TalkEvent) => (
											<li>
												<Link href={event.eventUrl}>{event.name}</Link> &mdash;{" "}
												{event.date}
												{event.talkUrl && (
													<>
														{" "}
														&mdash; <Link href={event.talkUrl}>Talk page</Link>
													</>
												)}
											</li>
										))}
								</ul>
							</li>
						))}
					</ul>
				) : (
					<p>No upcoming talks right now.</p>
				)
			}
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3 class="talks-sub-heading">Past Talks</h3>
			<lite-youtube
				videoid="IvyLMwMNU0g"
				playlistid="PL70YCHVvqVvxfJX9B81P-TjvbbKoXjegG"
			>
